    "body": "Uptime: Aquifer pid 660 up since ~15:23 UTC (aquifer_up_s 10836 at 18:23). No kills and no restarts so far (kills=0, restarts=0 in /events). The first kill -9 has not happened yet, so the flush-window case is untested. No prior reports exist (/reports returned null), so this is the baseline. /status/daily is null, and hourly history covers only 15:00-18:00, so there are no multi-day trends yet.\n\nHTTP ledger (cumulative): submitted 5,324,082; accepted 4,664,538; lost 0; lost_within_flush_window 0; stuck_over_24h 0; finished_without_webhook 97 (all in the 16:52 webhook-down window, 140s); failed_webhooks 2,056 (follows webhook down/503 modes); shed_429_503 643,544 (during bursts/ramps and 429 upstream); duplicate_webhooks 10 and webhooks_for_unknown_jobs 10, both unchanged since 15:00, so static, not growing; client_errors 15,956, all in the first 36 minutes, none since.\n\nWebSocket (ledger v2, which began at the 16:22 driver restart; the v0 ledger was discarded): lost_commands 27,803; messages_for_unknown_commands 172,164; commands_resent 286,571; duplicate_events 193,241. Hourly: 366 lost at 17:00, 27,208 at 18:00, 27,803 at 18:23. Unknown messages appeared in the 17:00 hour. I cannot tell from these pages whether Aquifer drops or mis-IDs commands, or whether the driver's resend/ID bookkeeping is wrong. Ruled out: unrecorded_commands 0 and handshake errors 0. Not ruled out: Aquifer dropping commands, or a harness bug.\n\nTrends: too short to call. Over 16:23-18:23 RSS ranged 262-455 MB, goroutines 1,552-7,717 (burst peaks), open fds 706-2,747, pebble 387-932 MB with 74-195 files. Accept p99 is 48-2,165 ms, with the 2,165 ms at 17:23 during recovery. Steady-phase e2e p99 is 14-37 s, which looks high for a healthy upstream, though the queue was backlogged by 429s. The harness looks healthy: minutes_target_unreachable 0, generator_saturated not raised, hourly summaries current, one driver gap of ~22 min (16:00-16:22, while Aquifer ran).\n\nOpen issue #39 (Pebble growth, filed 2026-10-11) is from the previous run. Current pebble is 915 MB, so it is not directly comparable.\n\nNext: (1) diff WS command IDs sent vs recorded vs completed for a few lost commands in /logs; (2) confirm whether the v0-to-v2 WS ledger change is the source of the unknown-message count; (3) schedule the first kill and check lost within the flush window; (4) keep watching the daily ramp ceiling once it exists."
